.TH WAVE-INSTALL 1 "" "MacWave" "MacWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-install \- Install a package, or one specific version of it.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave install <package>[@<version>] [flags]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Install a package, or one specific version of it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-C, \-\-continue
Resume an interrupted download (like curl -C -)
.TP
.B \-\-proxy <string>
HTTP/HTTPS proxy (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8080)
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-ssl
Skip SSL certificate verification (insecure)
.TP
.B \-\-limit\-rate <string>
Limit download speed (e.g. 200K, 1M, 5M)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-time <string>
Total time limit for the request (40s, 1min, 1min20s, 2h; bare numbers
are seconds)
.TP
.B \-\-connect\-timeout <string>
Give up if the handshake takes longer (like curl)
.TP
.B \-\-content\-time <string>
Give up if no data arrives for this long
.TP
.B \-\-unlink
Do not create or re-point the unversioned link
.TP
.B \-\-install\-from\-source
Download from the upstream URL in the index instead of MacWave's own
bottle store (dependencies follow the same rule)
.TP
.B \-F, \-\-force
Install anyway when the package declares a newer macOS than this machine
runs
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave install jq
wave install ffmpeg@6.1
wave install jq --limit-rate 1M
wave install jq --max-time=1min
wave install jq --install-from-source
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
